# Check every text file out with the endings it is stored with.
#
# Without this a clone on Windows takes core.autocrlf at its word and materialises the
# whole tree with CRLF, which the committed bytes never had. Nothing in the build reads
# an ending except gofmt, which refuses a CRLF file outright: a fresh clone therefore
# reports every Go file in the repository as unformatted, including the ones nobody has
# touched. The check that is supposed to catch a real fault answers with all of them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries carry no endings to convert.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.zip binary
*.wav binary
*.exe binary
